([Sidenote: Men paid for what they know--not for what they do]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Failure is more often chargeable to a refusal to learn by mistakes how) Tj T*
(to avoid them than it is in making them. Experience is a good teacher,) Tj T*
(but who can deny the value to be gained in learning from the) Tj T*
(experience of others, for we cannot all have the same experience or) Tj T*
(the same view of similar experiences. There are many pathways to) Tj T*
(success, but the road of individual experience is narrow and rugged.) Tj T*
(It is a commonly accepted fact that for every ten dollars a) Tj T*
(high-salaried man draws, he receives nine dollars for what he knows) Tj T*
(and one dollar for what he does. On the same basis the successful) Tj T*
(business man, employing a large force of other men, realizes that his) Tj T*
(own greatest worth, as applied to his affairs, lies not so much in) Tj T*
(what he can do himself as how much he can encourage his employes to) Tj T*
(do. In either case, his own personal knowledge is the power behind the) Tj T*
(throne.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Knowledge in excess of present needs necessary]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The man who would secure the largest net return from his individual) Tj T*
(effort in the field of endeavor, and he who would realize the greatest) Tj T*
(possible advantage from the efforts of those under his command must,) Tj T*
(of necessity, possess knowledge--indispensable perception far in) Tj T*
(excess of the needs of the moment. Discernment, like a bank account,) Tj T*
(soon runs out if it is overdrawn or if it is not continually) Tj T*
(replenished. In business the ?checking system? of knowledge is the) Tj T*
(sort of account that pays best--not the ?savings account system.?) Tj T*
(Knowledge that is simply corked up and allowed to accumulate cobwebs) Tj T*
(and rust can avail nothing. The sharpest vinegar is procured by) Tj T*
(constantly replenishing the old stock with new.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: 90% failures vs. 10% moneymakers]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reliable statistics prove that only about ten per cent of all people) Tj T*
(who engage in business are successful and make money; the other ninety) Tj T*
(per cent become insolvent and fail. That is, they do not actually) Tj T*
(encounter the sheriff, or go into the hands of a receiver, but they) Tj T*
(fail nevertheless to succeed in the sense of making money, and what) Tj T*
(other possible reason can anyone have for engaging in business if not) Tj T*
(to accumulate money?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
