(Why do so many fail? Ask any credit man and he will tell you that it) Tj T*
(is not because of the lack of capital, or other material resources,) Tj T*
(but it is due primarily to a lack of intellectual capacity, the sort) Tj T*
(of brains that dig and work and sweat until they find a way to) Tj T*
(accomplish things; brains that go to the bottom of things; brains that) Tj T*
(are always looking for better results; brains that never abandon a) Tj T*
(problem until they have found a way to solve it. A friend once told me) Tj T*
(that he inquired of the manager of a house employing some three) Tj T*
(hundred traveling men how many salesmen they had. The manager replied,) Tj T*
(?Three.? My friend asked, ?How?s that? I am told your force of) Tj T*
(traveling men numbers nearly three hundred.? ?Ah, that is quite) Tj T*
(different,? replied the manager; ?we have two hundred and ninety-seven) Tj T*
(traveling men, but only three salesmen.? Quite likely that manager?s) Tj T*
(estimate was intended to be taken figuratively rather than literally,) Tj T*
(but it serves to illustrate the fact that in this great United States) Tj T*
(there are millions of men, young, middle-aged and old, who are content) Tj T*
(to plod along in a mediocre sort of way, heedless or unmindful of the) Tj T*
(fact that opportunity, knowledge, possibilities, are calling, calling,) Tj T*
(calling to them to come up higher. There are hundreds of thousands of) Tj T*
(other men engaged in business who sit idly by while their trade, like) Tj T*
(the sands in the hour glass, slowly ebbs away, and eventually is) Tj T*
(absorbed by their more progressive business neighbors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Moneymaking and business literature]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is still another vast army of business men--salesmen, clerks and) Tj T*
(wage-earners of all classes--who are beginning to catch a glimpse of) Tj T*
(the dawning of a new business era, the greatest the world has ever) Tj T*
(known, an era impregnated with possibilities and opportunities for) Tj T*
(those who are ready with wicks trimmed and oil in their lamps. To the) Tj T*
(earnest latter class which is really desirous of profiting by the) Tj T*
(experience of others, there is no need of elaborating the) Tj T*
(possibilities embodied in this course of reading in Business) Tj T*
(Administration. This set of books, containing valuable business data) Tj T*
(on many subjects, thousands of pages telling the story of success) Tj T*
(illustrated by trained men whose names are respected everywhere, is) Tj T*
