(Show me the man who says he has no patience for such things, and I) Tj T*
(will show you a man, like the stroke oar and the lawn mower, who does) Tj T*
(not believe in moving forward in progress. Show me the man who says he) Tj T*
(has no time to read of new methods and principles, and I will show you) Tj T*
(the one who utterly fails to perceive that familiarity with business) Tj T*
(literature of this kind means pecuniary advancement. Show me the man) Tj T*
(who says he cannot afford to invest in such a set of books, and I will) Tj T*
(show you one who apparently CAN afford to waste his energy in) Tj T*
(misdirected effort--that energy and effort which are to every) Tj T*
(wage-earner and tradesman both his stock in trade and his invested) Tj T*
(capital.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Failures unnecessary]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Someone has said, ?There are three kinds of people in the world--the) Tj T*
(Can?ts, the Won?ts and the Wills. The first fail at everything; the) Tj T*
(second oppose everything; the third succeed at everything.? I would) Tj T*
(add a fourth kind--the largest class of all--the Don?t Trys, the) Tj T*
(?Oh-what?s-the-use,? ?It-doesn?t-interest-me? sort of people. Their) Tj T*
(name is legion; their fault is lack of confidence. Knowledge is the) Tj T*
(greatest inspiration of confidence to be found on earth. You may not) Tj T*
(personally be held in the hope-paralyzing bondage that produces the) Tj T*
(?Oh-what?s-the-use,? or ?I?m-not-interested? germ, but if you are not,) Tj T*
(you are exceptional. Most people are, and that is the reason that such) Tj T*
(persons are just about what luck, good fortune or chance make them,) Tj T*
(succeeding if fortune favors them, failing if they are left to depend) Tj T*
(upon their own resources. Result: Nine fail where one succeeds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is very fortunate, indeed, for most men that so much of their) Tj T*
(happiness depends upon success. There is nothing on earth quite so) Tj T*
(terrible to think of as failure, especially that due to lack of) Tj T*
(effort, unless possibly it be the failure of a man who lacks the) Tj T*
(courage or initiative to try to make the most of himself, and thus) Tj T*
(lets his best opportunities escape him. And this last is really the) Tj T*
(most pitiful thing that can befall a man. It is well enough to plan) Tj T*
(opportunities, but if we had the wisdom to take advantage of such) Tj T*
(opportunities as naturally come to us, results would more often be) Tj T*
(found in the balance on the right side of the ledger. And so I am of) Tj T*
(the opinion that a clear explanation of why a very large class of) Tj T*
