(Now the significant characteristics of such a manorial society were) Tj T*
(three. First, it was economically self-sufficient, that is,) Tj T*
(practically everything that was needed or was consumed on the manor) Tj T*
(was produced there. There was no need of intercourse with the outside) Tj T*
(world and there was little contact with it. Salt, iron, and millstones) Tj T*
(were almost the only things that the inhabitants of such a manor had) Tj T*
(to buy from outsiders. Consequently there was no production of goods) Tj T*
(for a market, little money, and almost no trade. The few things that) Tj T*
(were purchased were paid for at prices fixed by custom. Secondly,) Tj T*
(agriculture was carried on under a system of joint labor, and) Tj T*
(under customary methods which did not change from generation to            3) Tj T*
(generation. It is clear that as long as all the land of the manor was) Tj T*
(thrown together, for purposes of cultivation, into fields on which) Tj T*
(were planted wheat or barley or which lay fallow, no one individual) Tj T*
(could cultivate his land differently from his neighbors. Indeed, the) Tj T*
(holdings of the different tenants were not even separated by fences,) Tj T*
(but only by ridges of grass. On the land which lay fallow the cattle) Tj T*
(were turned out to graze; if any man had attempted to plant a new crop) Tj T*
(the third year, his neighbors? cattle would have devoured it under) Tj T*
(such a system. Production was regulated absolutely by custom, and no) Tj T*
(opportunity was given for the development of the inventiveness or) Tj T*
(initiative of the progressive individual. Thirdly, the tenants were) Tj T*
(personally unfree, that is, they did not have the liberty of moving) Tj T*
(freely from place to place, but were bound to the soil which they) Tj T*
(cultivated. A man could not freely choose either his occupation or his) Tj T*
(residence. There was no mobility or freedom of movement. Labor was) Tj T*
(wholly or partly compulsory, and on terms rigidly fixed by custom or) Tj T*
(by superior authority.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
