(contrast our own of the twentieth century. The chief characteristics) Tj T*
(of the modern industrial system are the institutions of private) Tj T*
(property, of competition, and of personal liberty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The institution of private property is so familiar to us and so) Tj T*
(fundamental in modern economic life, that we commonly regard it as) Tj T*
(a natural right. Nevertheless, private property, like most other           4) Tj T*
(economic institutions, is the result of a long evolution. Primitive) Tj T*
(man can hardly have had the conception of private property, and when) Tj T*
(it did begin to emerge, it was at first confined to movables. Indeed) Tj T*
(we may say that on the mediaeval English manor the private ownership) Tj T*
(of land did not yet exist in the modern sense. It was found however) Tj T*
(that, when each cultivator was permitted to fence in his holding and) Tj T*
(to call it his own, he cultivated it much more carefully and produced) Tj T*
(much more. Inclosure led to private property in land and to individual) Tj T*
(freedom in its use. Today in the United States the possession and) Tj T*
(transfer of landed property is almost as easy as that of movables.) Tj T*
(Private property must be justified on the ground of social utility,) Tj T*
(because under this method of control so much more is produced than) Tj T*
(under any system of commercial ownership yet tried. But there are not) Tj T*
(wanting objectors who contend that limits should be placed upon this) Tj T*
(institution, and that the right of use, of bequest, and possibly of) Tj T*
(unlimited acquisition should be brought under social control. The) Tj T*
(beneficence of private property turns largely upon the existence of) Tj T*
(competition and individual liberty and to these we must now turn.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Competition is defined as ?the act of seeking or endeavoring to gain) Tj T*
(what another is endeavoring to gain at the same time.? But competition) Tj T*
(in modern industrial life is not merely a struggle to appropriate an) Tj T*
(existing good. The very contest, as over the control of a market, may) Tj T*
(and probably will lead to cheaper and larger production, and thus to) Tj T*
(the benefit of society. Competition is a selective process in our) Tj T*
(modern economic society, and through it we have the survival of the) Tj T*
(fittest. ?Competition,? so runs the proverb, ?is the soul of trade.?) Tj T*
(There is, to be sure, a dark side to the picture, for economic) Tj T*
(competition involves the defeat of the weaker party, but this does not) Tj T*
(necessarily mean his destruction, for his very failure may sharpen         5) Tj T*
(his faculties and secure his ultimate success, or at worst he may find) Tj T*
(employment under his successful rival. But here again it is being) Tj T*
(urged that competition is brutal and that we should go back to the) Tj T*
(mediaeval method of regulation by custom, or resort to combination and) Tj T*
(monopoly. We are now witnessing experiments in both directions, but) Tj T*
(competition still remains the controlling force of modern economic) Tj T*
(society, and bids fair to continue so. It should however be the) Tj T*
(function of society to raise the ethical level of competition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
