(Before the introduction of the factory system, under the so-called) Tj T*
(?domestic? system of industry, the laborer carried on his work in his) Tj T*
(own home, where he provided the raw material, owned his own tools,) Tj T*
(furnished the motive power--his muscles--and was his own master. Today) Tj T*
(every one of these conditions is changed--the work is carried on in) Tj T*
(the factory, the raw material, the tools, the motive power are all) Tj T*
(provided by the capitalist, the laborer contributing only his own more) Tj T*
(or less skilled labor, while the conditions under which he carries on) Tj T*
(his work are largely determined for him. He is no longer his own) Tj T*
(master. To protect himself against the growing power of capital the) Tj T*
(worker has organized with his fellows into trade unions. These seek to) Tj T*
(meet the monopolistic power of capital by exerting a monopolistic) Tj T*
(control over labor. While they realize that modern productive) Tj T*
(processes cannot be carried on without capital, they also insist that) Tj T*
(labor is equally essential. They claim that capital has received more) Tj T*
(than its fair share of their joint production and has exploited labor;) Tj T*
(consequently they insist that labor must now demand its just reward) Tj T*
(and enforce the claim by strikes and by raising wages. To enforce) Tj T*
(their monopoly, the policy of the closed shop is often enforced. The) Tj T*
(interests of capital and labor have thus often been made to appear) Tj T*
(antagonistic instead of complementary to one another. Frequently in) Tj T*
(their struggles the interests of the consumer have been entirely lost) Tj T*
(sight of.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These conflicts in the productive processes of modern economic society) Tj T*
(have led many people to look to the state as the regulator of industry     8) Tj T*
(and to invoke state aid or state interference along many lines.) Tj T*
(Maladjustments in the labor contract, mistaken production, leading) Tj T*
(perhaps to speculation and financial panics, abuses of power by) Tj T*
(corporate interests, discriminations by railroads, and similar) Tj T*
(irregularities are made the excuse for an appeal to state authority.) Tj T*
(Some would even go so far as to have the state take over and manage) Tj T*
(all productive enterprises; but socialism is as yet a protest rather) Tj T*
(than a constructive force. In the last analysis the state is the) Tj T*
(regulator of all industrial undertakings, for they all concern) Tj T*
(society. The state must hold the balance even and see that fair play) Tj T*
(is given to all groups and all classes; but the greatest amount of) Tj T*
(freedom compatible with economic justice must be sought for. It is a) Tj T*
(difficult question how far the state must interfere in the conduct or) Tj T*
(management of industrial enterprises in order to secure social) Tj T*
(justice. There is a decided tendency at present to a strengthening of) Tj T*
(the regulative power of the state for the protection of the weaker) Tj T*
(classes of society. And yet on the whole the institution of private) Tj T*
(property, free competition, and a maximum of individual liberty remain) Tj T*
(the fundamental conditions of our economic life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
