(VII. THE MODERN WAGE SYSTEM.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have already characterized the modern system of industry as) Tj T*
(capitalistic, that is, as involving the use of expensive and complex) Tj T*
(machinery in factories under the control of the capitalist managers of) Tj T*
(industry. As we have seen, such a system has caused an enormous) Tj T*
(increase in the production of wealth; it has also raised the general) Tj T*
(standard of comfort and the level of wages, and has relieved labor to) Tj T*
(a considerable extent of the deadly strain of hard manual toil that) Tj T*
(was characteristic of preceding systems. The factory system, under) Tj T*
(which capitalistic production is now carried on, may also fairly be) Tj T*
(credited with other beneficial results: as steadiness and punctuality     61) Tj T*
(are essential, it has on the whole led to increased sobriety and) Tj T*
(temperance; the work in general is healthier, being performed under) Tj T*
(better sanitary conditions than under the old domestic system; the) Tj T*
(intellectual status of the workingman has been raised, as vastly more) Tj T*
(intelligence is required of a skilled machine operator than of the) Tj T*
(old-time hand laborer; and finally the general well-being of the) Tj T*
(working class has been improved, as they have shared in the larger) Tj T*
(production made possible by machine methods. But, on the other hand,) Tj T*
(the new processes and methods have been accompanied by great abuses,) Tj T*
(though never so great in this country as in England. Long hours, the) Tj T*
(employment of women and children, the weakened economic position of) Tj T*
(the laborer, fluctuations in production, liability to be without) Tj T*
(employment, industrial accidents, the abolition of personal ties) Tj T*
(between employer and employe, the crowding of workmen into a small) Tj T*
(space to work by day and their concentration in city tenements by) Tj T*
(night--these are some of the problems for which the factory system) Tj T*
(must be held responsible. The condition and position of labor have) Tj T*
(been vitally affected. So far we have considered mainly the problems) Tj T*
(connected with the organization and use of capital. We must now take) Tj T*
(up the various questions connected with the relation of labor to) Tj T*
(capital and to the capitalistic system of production.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
