() Tj T*
(Another characteristic of modern industry from the labor point of view) Tj T*
(is the existence not merely of a wage-earning class, but, more) Tj T*
(fundamental, of the wage system. ?It is characteristic of the modern) Tj T*
(industrial system,? writes President Hadley,[10] ?that a laborer who) Tj T*
(owns no capital, though nominally free to do what he pleases, must) Tj T*
(actually find some property owner who will give him enough to keep him) Tj T*
(alive during the period which must elapse between the rendering of the) Tj T*
(labor and the sale of the finished product. Under such circumstances,) Tj T*
(the laborer almost inevitably submits to the direction of the property) Tj T*
(owner in deciding how his labor shall be applied. Laborers without) Tj T*
(capital must necessarily work on this basis; even those who have small) Tj T*
(amounts of capital habitually do so. Such advances of capital are) Tj T*
(known as wages.? Here we have the essence of the wage system in a nut) Tj T*
(shell. The laborer sells his labor to an employer for a stipulated) Tj T*
(wage. He has a commodity, his labor, consisting of a certain amount of) Tj T*
(strength and skill, which he is free to dispose of on the market to) Tj T*
(the best advantage, as the owner of any other commodity might do.) Tj T*
