(some cases, as the iron and steel workers, where there is a regular       94) Tj T*
(two months? shut-down to make repairs, and the building trades where) Tj T*
(the inclemency of the weather usually prevents work during the winter,) Tj T*
(the lack of employment may be regarded as a vacation rather than a) Tj T*
(hardship, for the rates of pay are high enough during the remaining) Tj T*
(months to offset those of idleness. In other cases, however, as in) Tj T*
(coal-mining, there is a large reserve army of workers on hand and) Tj T*
(employment is secured for only one-half to two-thirds the time. In) Tj T*
(1900, when the average number of days of employment was larger than it) Tj T*
(had been in ten years, the bituminous miners were employed only 234) Tj T*
(days and the anthracite miners only 166 days in the year. This) Tj T*
(indicates a very bad organization of the industry. The same thing was) Tj T*
(formerly true of the London dockyards, where there was a reserve army) Tj T*
(of some 4,000 surplus workers. Of course the effect of this is to) Tj T*
(depress wages. The clothing trade is subject to seasonal fluctuations) Tj T*
(and the caprice of fashion, and offers very irregular employment.) Tj T*
(Machinery and improved processes were frequently spoken of by) Tj T*
(witnesses before the Industrial Commission as the leading cause of) Tj T*
(unemployment. If the general conditions of business are good at the) Tj T*
(time of the first introduction of machinery the displaced laborer is) Tj T*
(reabsorbed again and the hardship is not so noticeable. But if it) Tj T*
(coincides with a period of business depression the introduction of) Tj T*
(machinery appears to be the cause of a large displacement of labor,) Tj T*
(which might more truly be ascribed to industrial depression. This last) Tj T*
(cause is responsible for enormous suffering among the laboring) Tj T*
(classes, for the method oftenest resorted to by industrial enterprises) Tj T*
(to reduce expenses is the wholesale discharge of laborers, who are) Tj T*
(thus made to bear the burden of industrial disorganization. This was) Tj T*
(well illustrated by the economies effected by the railroads in the) Tj T*
(year 1908, in their general reduction of the labor force and of wages.) Tj T*
(But even in good years the inconstancy of employment is startling. In     95) Tj T*
(the four years 1897-1900 the men in trade unions in New York State) Tj T*
(lost 16.2 per cent of their time from unemployment, which is almost) Tj T*
