(So far we have discussed for the most part those economic problems) Tj T*
(that center round the production of wealth, such as the use of natural) Tj T*
(resources, large-scale production, trusts and monopolies, labor) Tj T*
(organizations, unemployment, industrial education and co-operation.) Tj T*
(Now we shall consider briefly a few of the problems that are connected) Tj T*
(with the distribution of wealth. Professor Blockmar[38] says that the) Tj T*
(three great problems of economic society are: ?First, how to create) Tj T*
(the largest amount of utilities or wealth; second, how justly to) Tj T*
(divide this amount; and third, how to make the product minister to the) Tj T*
(permanent rather than to the transient well-being of society.? The) Tj T*
(first problem we have already discussed; the second forms the subject) Tj T*
(of the present section; while the third will be taken up in the next) Tj T*
(section. Within the last century the center of interest in the) Tj T*
(practical application of economic principles has decidedly shifted) Tj T*
(from production to distribution. The earlier writers in economics, as) Tj T*
(shown in the mercantile lists of the seventeenth and eighteenth) Tj T*
(centuries, even Adam Smith, were chiefly interested in methods of) Tj T*
(increasing a nation?s wealth. With the introduction of the factory) Tj T*
(system and the opening up of vast natural resources by improvements in) Tj T*
(mining and transportation, the production of wealth has enormously) Tj T*
(increased, and now the question of the method of its distribution or) Tj T*
(division is felt to be more pressing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Under the term distribution two different processes are included,) Tj T*
(which should be distinguished before going further. The first is) Tj T*
(called functional distribution, and concerns the distribution of the) Tj T*
(product of industry or the income of society, among the different) Tj T*
(factors of production. That is to say, land, labor, capital and          120) Tj T*
(managerial ability have contributed in varying degrees to the) Tj T*
(production of a certain amount of current wealth, and the problem of) Tj T*
(functional distribution is to ascertain how the net product resulting) Tj T*
(from these joint efforts is divided. How much goes to rent, how much) Tj T*
(to wages, how much to interest and how much to profits? The second) Tj T*
(kind of distribution is the division of the wealth of society among) Tj T*
(individuals or families; this is personal distribution, and raises the) Tj T*
(question of poverty and great wealth. In discussing these problems,) Tj T*
(however, we must remember that wealth production and distribution) Tj T*
(takes place in modern society under conditions imposed by the social) Tj T*
(order in which we live; these were defined as competition, private) Tj T*
(property and personal liberty. If any modifications of the processes) Tj T*
