(XIV. SAVING AND SPENDING.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The goal and purpose of all economic activities is the satisfaction of) Tj T*
(human wants. The object of production is consumption. We work because) Tj T*
(we desire and need various things which we can get only if we produce) Tj T*
(them or earn the money to buy them. In this section we take up some      128) Tj T*
(of the problems connected with the rational use or consumption of the) Tj T*
(wealth which is continually being produced. We have seen something of) Tj T*
(the conditions under which it is produced, and the manner in which it) Tj T*
(is distributed; we must now study the not less important subject of) Tj T*
(its application to human needs and desires. The great question is, how) Tj T*
(can we get the largest and most rational return for a given) Tj T*
(expenditure? Before trying to answer this question, it will be helpful) Tj T*
(to present a summary statement of actual expenditures in different) Tj T*
