(discovery of wagon roads through the air in the realm of) Tj T*
(transportation. Another argument advanced in favor of government paper) Tj T*
(money is that it would be possible by a scientific adjustment of the     141) Tj T*
(issues to regulate the amount of money in circulation and so to) Tj T*
(prevent all fluctuations in prices. Both contraction and inflation) Tj T*
(would be prevented and a cheap and yet ideal system of money would) Tj T*
(exist. Still others see in this form of money an instrument for the) Tj T*
(creation of wealth; this last argument simply results from a confusion) Tj T*
(of ideas and need not be dealt with. A sufficient answer to the other) Tj T*
(two is an appeal to the lesson of history: no government which has) Tj T*
(embarked upon the issue of paper money has ever been able to restrict) Tj T*
(the issues within reasonable limits; often it has led to national) Tj T*
(bankruptcy and the repudiation of the entire issues. The experience of) Tj T*
(the United States with the greenbacks has been more fortunate than) Tj T*
(that of many countries, but does not tempt to further experiment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The monetary situation in the United States today may be regarded as) Tj T*
(fairly well settled. Although we have a very heterogeneous assortment) Tj T*
(of different kinds of money, a fairly distinct sphere is allotted to) Tj T*
(each, and as the basis for all, the gold standard has been definitely) Tj T*
(established by law. Money of large denominations consists of gold and) Tj T*
(gold certificates \(lowest denomination, $20\), of greenbacks and) Tj T*
(national bank notes \(lowest denomination, $10, though one-third of) Tj T*
(bank notes may be $5\); the needs of retail trade are met by the issue) Tj T*
(of silver certificates and silver dollars, and of fractional currency.) Tj T*
(The system would be much simplified by the retirement and destruction) Tj T*
(of the $346,000,000 in greenbacks, but as there is now a fifty-per) Tj T*
(cent reserve in gold back of them, little danger need be apprehended) Tj T*
(from their presence. Many people have regarded the existence of some) Tj T*
($500,000,000 worth of silver dollars as a menace to the goodness of) Tj T*
(our money supply, but as the amount of gold in circulation increases) Tj T*
(the silver will form a constantly smaller percentage of the whole. It) Tj T*
(is a cumbersome and not very valuable asset of the Government, but       142) Tj T*
(is now almost powerless for good or ill.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Important as is the subject of money and essential as is the need of a) Tj T*
(standard of undoubted goodness, it is overshadowed in practical) Tj T*
(significance by the problems of banking and credit. An investigation) Tj T*
(by the Comptroller of the Currency some years ago showed that over 90) Tj T*
(per cent of the receipts of the national banks consisted of credit) Tj T*
(instruments, while probably 60 per cent of the trade of the country) Tj T*
(was carried on by credit rather than by cash transactions. A credit) Tj T*
(transaction is a transfer of goods or money for a future equivalent;) Tj T*
(the element of time is introduced. This makes possible an enormous) Tj T*
(increase in the number of exchanges and obviates the necessity, to a) Tj T*
(large extent, of using money. Most of us enjoy personal credit, which) Tj T*
(is limited only by our ability to persuade other people to trust in) Tj T*
(us. But this power of purchasing things without immediate payment must) Tj T*
(be made readily available if the ordinary business man is to make use) Tj T*
(of it. This is done through the medium of a bank, whose business it is) Tj T*
(to discount the notes of its customers, which in turn is based upon) Tj T*
(confidence in their prospective earnings. The bank credit thus) Tj T*
