(obtained may be transferred by means of checks to other persons and to) Tj T*
(other banks. It is the most fluid and volatile means of payment yet) Tj T*
(devised, and is subject to dangers and abuses. In the last analysis) Tj T*
(business based upon such a system of credit rests upon confidence in) Tj T*
(the honesty of individuals and in the enforcement of the law governing) Tj T*
(contracts, and also in the ability of those who have pledged) Tj T*
(themselves to future payment to make good their obligations. In times) Tj T*
(of panic credit fails and resort is had to money.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fundamental institution in our credit economy is the bank, and it) Tj T*
(is therefore essential that it be thoroughly safe and responsive to) Tj T*
(the needs of the business world. A bank may furnish its customers        143) Tj T*
(with the ready means of payment they need in exchange for their future) Tj T*
(promises either in the form of bank notes or bank credit. The former) Tj T*
(are more largely used on the continent of Europe and in rural) Tj T*
(districts in this country, the latter by England and the United) Tj T*
(States, especially in the cities. The preference for one or the other) Tj T*
(seems to be a matter of geography. The issue of bank notes has been) Tj T*
(very carefully safeguarded since the establishment of the national) Tj T*
(banking system in 1863. They are based upon the purchase of government) Tj T*
(bonds and are absolutely safe. They lack, however, one essential) Tj T*
(quality of good bank money in that they are quite inelastic. That is) Tj T*
(to say, the amount of bank notes in circulation does not vary) Tj T*
(according to the needs of business, increasing to meet an increased) Tj T*
(demand, and then declining again when the demand has passed. Being) Tj T*
(based upon government bonds and not upon the value of business assets,) Tj T*
(they vary in amount only with the price of the former and not at all) Tj T*
(with the volume of the latter.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The main practical problem connected with our banking system is,) Tj T*
(therefore, to find some other basis for the issue of bank notes,) Tj T*
(especially as it is not desirable to maintain a permanent bonded) Tj T*
(indebtedness solely for this purpose. Various suggestions have been) Tj T*
(made, as the establishment of a central bank with sole power of issue,) Tj T*
(like the government banks in European countries. This is a favorite) Tj T*
(proposal with the big bankers, but is unlikely to be adopted as it is) Tj T*
(directly contrary to the spirit of the existing system. The Canadian) Tj T*
(system is held up as a model, with its system of branch banking and 5) Tj T*
(per cent safety fund for the redemption of the notes of failed banks.) Tj T*
(Curiously enough this was copied after the system in operation in New) Tj T*
(York State, which was nipped in the bud by some early mistakes and by) Tj T*
(the development of the national banking system. It works admirably in) Tj T*
(Canada and is well worth careful study. The plan of asset currency       144) Tj T*
(is another suggestion, according to which bank notes should be issued) Tj T*
(up to a certain percentage of the resources of the bank, but without) Tj T*
(pledging any specific property for their redemption as is done in the) Tj T*
(case of the national banks at present. It has finally been urged that) Tj T*
(our present bond deposit system should be modified by substituting) Tj T*
(state, municipal, railroad, or industrial bonds for those of the) Tj T*
(Federal Government, but that in other respects the system should be) Tj T*
(left intact. We may look for legislation along one or another of these) Tj T*
(lines in the next few years, as the subject is an urgent one whose) Tj T*
