(solution cannot long be postponed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another problem is connected with the money reserves that the banks) Tj T*
(are required by law to keep on hand in order to meet demand) Tj T*
(liabilities. Under the national system in the United States the) Tj T*
(country banks may deposit three-fifths of their lawful reserves with) Tj T*
(banks in reserve cities, and these banks in turn may deposit one-half) Tj T*
(of their reserves in banks in central reserve cities \(New York,) Tj T*
(Chicago, and St. Louis\). Thus there is a massing, under this system,) Tj T*
(of the bank reserves of the country in the city of New York, and) Tj T*
(within that city in some twenty banks. While there is great economy in) Tj T*
(such a system the concentration of reserves is certainly attended by) Tj T*
(great dangers, not the least of which is its use by speculative) Tj T*
(influences in the New York money market, as a great part of it is) Tj T*
(loaned out to speculators on call.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Still another practical problem connected with the monetary and) Tj T*
(banking system of the United States is that of the independent) Tj T*
(treasury system. The Federal Government is to a large extent its own) Tj T*
(banker; it collects, disburses its revenue and keeps its money in its) Tj T*
(own vaults; it even, as we have seen, issues paper money and keeps a) Tj T*
(reserve therefor. By its action in withdrawing large amounts of money) Tj T*
(from use, or on the other hand making large disbursements, it can and    145) Tj T*
(does affect the money market vitally and sometimes disastrously. While) Tj T*
(it is permitted to deposit funds in selected national banks and has) Tj T*
(recently made increasing use of this privilege, thus correlating in a) Tj T*
(measure the reserves of the Government and the needs of the business) Tj T*
(community, it is held by most students that the independent treasury) Tj T*
(system should be abolished, and that the banks should act as the) Tj T*
(intermediaries between the Government and the people in the collection) Tj T*
(and expenditure of its funds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(So far we have been discussing commercial banks, but there is another) Tj T*
(kind of institution which goes by the same name but serves quite a) Tj T*
(different purpose, namely, the savings bank. The essential and almost) Tj T*
(the only requirement of such an institution is safety. As we have) Tj T*
(seen, it is not only desirable for personal reasons to inculcate) Tj T*
(habits of saving and thrift in individuals, but it is also necessary) Tj T*
(to secure the accumulation of capital needed in modern industry. It is) Tj T*
(therefore important that such institutions should be widespread,) Tj T*
(accessible, and thoroughly trusted. These requirements seem to be best) Tj T*
(fulfilled by the postal savings banks in England and elsewhere, which) Tj T*
(have led to a great increase in savings on the part of the people. The) Tj T*
(introduction of such a system in the United States is greatly to be) Tj T*
(desired.) Tj T*
