(branch of commerce. Coal, lumber, cotton, and similar bulky) Tj T*
(commodities constitute the chief items entering into the coastwise) Tj T*
(trade. The tonnage of American vessels engaged in the foreign trade,) Tj T*
(on the other hand, has shown a steady decline ever since the outbreak) Tj T*
(of the Civil War. Foreign vessels today carry fully 90 per cent of the) Tj T*
(foreign commerce of the United States. The causes of this decline are) Tj T*
(economic rather than political, for American legislation has on the) Tj T*
(whole been very liberal to the shipping interests. At the time the) Tj T*
(western part of our country began to be opened up and its great) Tj T*
(resources exploited, our merchant marine was one of the best in the      153) Tj T*
(world. But now the other opportunities for the investment of capital) Tj T*
(were so profitable and alluring, and the need of it so great, that all) Tj T*
(the available labor and capital of the American people began to be) Tj T*
(devoted to the development of their internal resources. A nation) Tj T*
(cannot do everything with equal advantage at the same time any more) Tj T*
(than an individual can. Accordingly we began to withdraw our capital) Tj T*
(from shipping and devote it to agriculture, mining, manufacturing,) Tj T*
