(then, if we are to render sound judgment on these questions, to have a) Tj T*
(clear opinion as to the proper sphere of government action, as to how) Tj T*
(far the State should interfere in the economic activities of private) Tj T*
(individuals. We cannot do better than to state first the main) Tj T*
(functions of a modern state. The modern industrial system, as we saw) Tj T*
(in the first section, is based upon certain fundamental) Tj T*
(institutions--personal liberty, competition, and private property. The) Tj T*
(first function of government is to guarantee to every individual the) Tj T*
(rights of freedom, property, and contract; this involves the) Tj T*
(maintenance of peace and order. These are often spoken of as ?natural) Tj T*
(rights?; rather they are rational rights, based upon expediency and) Tj T*
(human welfare, and are created and maintained by society. Without the) Tj T*
(constant support and intervention of government they would possess       164) Tj T*
(little reality or significance. But in addition to guaranteeing these) Tj T*
(fundamental institutions, modern governments grant individuals certain) Tj T*
(privileges, as patents, copyrights, trade-marks, franchises, etc.,) Tj T*
(designed to stimulate the economic activity of individuals.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A second group of functions undertaken by the modern state is) Tj T*
(regulative. As we have seen, laws are made regulating the freedom of) Tj T*
(contract, the conditions of labor, the conduct of business, methods of) Tj T*
(banking and transportation, etc. The terms under which competitive) Tj T*
(business may be conducted are laid down, and while freedom of industry) Tj T*
(prevails for every individual it is only on condition that he conforms) Tj T*
(to the rules of the game thus prescribed. But the conditions are not) Tj T*
(merely restrictive; sometimes they are designed to promote enterprise,) Tj T*
(as in the case of gifts, subsidies, protective duties, etc. In all) Tj T*
(these ways the State interferes with the action of perfectly free) Tj T*
(competition for the purpose of securing better or more equitable) Tj T*
(conditions. A third group of functions embraces the direct) Tj T*
(participation in industry by the Government itself, as the) Tj T*
(post-office, gas, electric, and water works, canals, roads, sewers,) Tj T*
(parks, etc. In other countries, when the functions of government are) Tj T*
(more extended than in the United States, it conducts railroads,) Tj T*
(telegraph and telephone systems, tenements, pawn shops, theaters,) Tj T*
(industrial insurance, or various other activities. The line which) Tj T*
(divides public from private enterprise varies greatly in different) Tj T*
(countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This raises the general question, how far is it desirable that the) Tj T*
(economic functions of government should extend? As to the necessity of) Tj T*
(state activity in some form there can be no doubt. Production,) Tj T*
(exchange, distribution, and to a smaller extent consumption, are all) Tj T*
(social processes; they concern the whole of society, and must be) Tj T*
(brought under social control. Montesquieu laid down the proposition) Tj T*
(in the middle of the eighteenth century that taxes invariably            165) Tj T*
(increase with the growth of liberty. Historically this has been) Tj T*
(verified: the development of freedom in government and industry has) Tj T*
(meant the realization of self-restraint by the imposition of) Tj T*
(regulative law. But the modern State has gone further than this: it) Tj T*
(has realized the necessity of taking an active part in modern) Tj T*
(industrial life, for the equalization of the terms of competition, the) Tj T*
