(anarchism contemplates an ideal state of perfect freedom, in which the) Tj T*
(State, the coercive exercise of authority by man over man, would not) Tj T*
(exist. According to this theory only the individual has rights; there) Tj T*
(is no more divinity of right in a majority than there is in kings.) Tj T*
(Government is an invasion of the right of the individual to do as he) Tj T*
(will, and should be abolished; with its abolition would vanish the) Tj T*
(various moral, social, and industrial evils to which it has given) Tj T*
(rise, and human society would develop on a higher plane. Stated in its) Tj T*
(extreme form anarchism is evidently too ideal for frail human nature) Tj T*
(as at present constituted. Of more practical importance has been the) Tj T*
(theory of extreme individualism as set forth by Herbert Spencer--a) Tj T*
(view designated by Huxley as the night-watchman theory of the State.) Tj T*
(According to this the functions of government should be limited to       166) Tj T*
(the protection of life and property and the enforcement of contracts,) Tj T*
(but should not include such things as education, regulation of) Tj T*
(industry, local improvements, charities, coinage, etc. Private) Tj T*
(initiative and competition are trusted to supply these things, while) Tj T*
(the economic harmony of the interests of each individual with those of) Tj T*
(society will prevent any wrong from being done. The keynote of the) Tj T*
(whole theory lies in the view that government is an evil, though a) Tj T*
(necessary one, and should consequently be restricted. Adam Smith?s) Tj T*
(system of ?national liberty? went somewhat further, as it added to the) Tj T*
(three functions named above, the construction of public works and) Tj T*
(buildings, etc.; but it excluded such activities as education and the) Tj T*
(civil courts, which we regard as most suited to government management.) Tj T*
(This theory had its origin in the reaction against the undue) Tj T*
(interference with industry by the Government under mercantilism and) Tj T*
(had thus a historic justification and value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The theory most generally held by economists and writers in the United) Tj T*
(States is probably the modified individualism set forth by John Stuart) Tj T*
(Mill. According to him, freedom of industry or ?laissez faire should) Tj T*
(be the general practice; every departure from it, unless required by) Tj T*
(some great good, is a certain evil.? Industry, he said, should be left) Tj T*
(to individuals and the Government should never interfere unless there) Tj T*
(is an antagonism between social and private interests. Individuals) Tj T*
(following their own interests will always conduct business better than) Tj T*
(the Government, which is inefficient, corrupt, and can fall back on) Tj T*
(taxation to cover its mistakes. Individualism should therefore be the) Tj T*
