(IV. CAPITAL IN MANUFACTURING.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another factor which entered into the modern system of production, and) Tj T*
(a very important one, was that of capital. The factory could not be) Tj T*
(established or operated without considerable amounts of money or its) Tj T*
(equivalent, credit. The machinery which transformed the raw material) Tj T*
(into the finished product, the material itself, the very buildings in) Tj T*
(which the work was performed, the payment for the transportation which) Tj T*
(brought it together, the wages of the men and women engaged in the) Tj T*
(work, all required capital, and in large sums. The accumulation of) Tj T*
(this capital, its management, the keeping of accounts of cost of) Tj T*
(material and labor and of the finished product, required financial) Tj T*
(skill and acquaintance in the markets in which this capital could be) Tj T*
(obtained; for often the sums required were in excess of the quantity) Tj T*
(possessed by the individual who had invested his all in the buildings) Tj T*
(and machinery, and must needs borrow of some other capitalist the) Tj T*
(additional sums required for purchasing material and paying the wages) Tj T*
(of his workmen. Sometimes the owner of the capital preferred to supply) Tj T*
(it and take a proportionate share in the earnings of the factory, and) Tj T*
(thus developed the company. Then, as the business grew and the) Tj T*
(investments of various men in a single establishment increased, it) Tj T*
(became necessary for them to take an active share in the management      215) Tj T*
(either in person or by representatives who became known as the) Tj T*
(?directors? of the work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus arose the successors of the individual manufacturer, the company,) Tj T*
(and the corporation. Man must die and the death of an individual) Tj T*
(manufacturer, or the manager of a manufacturing firm or partnership,) Tj T*
(must affect disadvantageously the interests of the factory and its) Tj T*
(employes. Thus the importance of organizations which would continue) Tj T*
