(direct competition with others in their own line of manufacture. If) Tj T*
(the market for their product was good they demanded higher prices. If) Tj T*
(there was an oversupply they sold for whatever profit they could get,) Tj T*
(or if necessary at cost or even lower than cost, in order to prevent) Tj T*
(accumulations of stocks or the closing of their factories. The) Tj T*
(competition thus grew intense. In order to dispose of their goods they) Tj T*
(must put many salesmen into the field, they must advertise freely,       223) Tj T*
(and often their orders came from such distances that the cost of) Tj T*
(delivery formed a large percentage of the cost of the goods by the) Tj T*
