(This competition of one manufacturer with another making the same line) Tj T*
(of goods was not only expensive but resulted in working at cross) Tj T*
(purposes in many ways, and in loss of energy and money. So certain of) Tj T*
(the companies or corporations engaged in like industries began to make) Tj T*
(agreements among themselves by which they could co-operate in) Tj T*
(distributing their supplies to a given field and reduce the expenses) Tj T*
(of supplying that field. It was argued that the people of any section) Tj T*
(would only use a given amount of any standard product, and that the) Tj T*
(expense which the various manufacturers were incurring in competing) Tj T*
(among themselves for their respective shares in that trade might be) Tj T*
(materially reduced by an agreement through which the extraordinary) Tj T*
(efforts to sell in competition with each other should be abandoned and) Tj T*
(each manufacturer receive the share of the sales to which his) Tj T*
(proportion of production would entitle him. Not only would this reduce) Tj T*
(unnecessary expenses but it would in some degree render possible the) Tj T*
(maintenance of prices as they might be mutually agreed upon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first steps in combinations or agreements of this sort are known) Tj T*
(as ?pools.? ?This form of agreement,? says J. Russell Smith, ?provides) Tj T*
(that each of the makers of a certain material for a certain territory) Tj T*
(should make a stipulated proportion of the product to be sold at an) Tj T*
(agreed price. If a factory made more than its share the owner made a) Tj T*
(cash payment to the pool and the money went to some manufacturer who) Tj T*
(had made less than his share. The weak spot of these pools was their) Tj T*
(absolute lack of power of coercion and that no member had faith in the) Tj T*
(others.? Often members took advantage of technicalities to violate the) Tj T*
(spirit of the agreement, and the agreements were short-lived. The        224) Tj T*
(system, while it is still working satisfactorily in Germany under the) Tj T*
(name of the ?cartel,? failed to give satisfactory results in the) Tj T*
(United States, and also met with disaster in the fact that the courts) Tj T*
(held it to be a combination in restraint of trade and therefore) Tj T*
(unlawful.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
