(The advantages of this combination over competition are summed up by) Tj T*
(the Encyclopedia Britannica, in its 1902 edition, as follows: \(1\) The) Tj T*
(cost of selling may be greatly lessened; \(2\) the salaries of) Tj T*
(commercial travelers and their traveling expenses can be largely) Tj T*
(reduced; \(3\) if different manufacturing establishments, scattered) Tj T*
(throughout the country, are brought under one management it will be) Tj T*
(possible for orders for goods to be distributed so that goods can be) Tj T*
(dispatched to customers in each case from the nearest establishment) Tj T*
(and freight expenses reduced; \(4\) when several establishments are) Tj T*
(combined the most skillful of the managers can be selected for the) Tj T*
(general manager; \(5\) each business manager is likely to have some) Tj T*
(special excellence in his methods of management, and by combining the) Tj T*
(establishments it is possible to so distribute this managerial skill) Tj T*
(as to give to each branch of the work the man best suited to its) Tj T*
(conduct; \(6\) it is also possible to distribute the various branches of) Tj T*
(the manufacturing to the various mills or factories of the combination) Tj T*
(best suited for that particular branch of the work; \(7\) the advantages) Tj T*
(of unifying in one establishment the machinery of selling the product) Tj T*
(of all; \(8\) the ability of an establishment to fill large orders on) Tj T*
(short notice gains and retains business; \(9\) the great financial and) Tj T*
(business strength and skill of the combined organization gives it) Tj T*
(special facilities for pushing its goods into foreign markets, as is) Tj T*
(shown by the success abroad of the Standard Oil Company, and the         226) Tj T*
(American Tobacco Company; \(10\) better facilities for dealing with) Tj T*
(credits and thus aiding the business community.) Tj T*
