<< /Length 3655 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(of the excessive cost of the increased amount of Portland cement. It) Tj T*
(is said, that a retaining wall of all concrete would have cost about) Tj T*
($600 per linear foot. Reinforced concrete costs about $58 per foot.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Steel is used, not merely as a reinforcement, but as the material of) Tj T*
(forms. Used thus, it may, at times, not only retain the concrete in) Tj T*
(position but also prevent the action of the surrounding soil or water.) Tj T*
(The possibility of using steel for forms depends largely upon the fact) Tj T*
(that many applications of concrete are becoming standardized rapidly.) Tj T*
(Thus is permitted a re-use of the steel form that justifies the) Tj T*
