(Deductions from Visits of Inspection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The deductions made from the visits in 1906 were as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The plants as a whole are giving remarkable satisfaction) Tj T*
(considering the very brief period of development that has passed since) Tj T*
(the introduction of this type of power.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. The most serious difficulty seems to arise from the lack of) Tj T*
(competent operators to run the plants rather than from defects or) Tj T*
(troubles in the plants themselves.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Incompetent salesmen are undoubtedly to blame for serious) Tj T*
(misrepresentations and misunderstandings.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. The neglect shown by some manufacturers in respect to their plants) Tj T*
(after they are installed and paid for has not been farsighted, and the) Tj T*
(failure of the manufacturers to give the purchasers or operators of      365) Tj T*
(plants full information regarding their construction and method of) Tj T*
(operating has certainly been detrimental to the business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
