(Centralization of Power Development and Distribution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Central stations for power and lighting are springing up all over the) Tj T*
(country. Electric lights are now in general use in towns numbering) Tj T*
(their population by hundreds only. Electric transmission for) Tj T*
(street-railway service is practically universal and electric power for) Tj T*
(shop drive is in great demand. The substitution of the electric) Tj T*
(locomotive for the steam locomotive for terminal service and even for) Tj T*
(line duty by several leading railway systems is no longer a mere) Tj T*
(expectation but is an every-day working reality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These changes and developments in every section are, to a large) Tj T*
(extent, tending to do away with the individual small steam equipment,) Tj T*
(whether stationary or locomotive, and are bringing to the front the) Tj T*
(central power station, ranging in size from lighting and pumping) Tj T*
(plants of less than 100 horsepower in the smaller towns to those of) Tj T*
(100,000 horsepower or more required to meet metropolitan demands.        366) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(European Examples of Advantageous Location.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the development of central power plants and the reduction of the) Tj T*
(cost of power, the producer-gas power plant is an important factor. In) Tj T*
(this connection the question of locating such plants directly at the) Tj T*
(mines is well worth careful and unbiased attention in the engineering) Tj T*
(profession. The advantages to be derived from such a location have) Tj T*
(already attracted the commercial interests of Europe. As examples) Tj T*
(worthy of thoughtful consideration, the general conditions of) Tj T*
(operation of three typical European installations are here described:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Plant A.--This plant, although not situated directly at the mines, is) Tj T*
(but a short distance away, and the company owning the plant also owns) Tj T*
(the mines from which the fuel is secured. The plant is of the Mond) Tj T*
(by-product type and consists of eight pressure producers of 2,500) Tj T*
(horsepower each. The fuel used is a run-of-mine bituminous coal said) Tj T*
(to contain 8 to 9 per cent ash and 1 to 2 per cent sulphur. This would) Tj T*
(indicate that they are utilizing the best grades of coal from their) Tj T*
(own mine in the local gas plant and allowing the lower grades to) Tj T*
