(twenty-four hours a day, seven days a week, for two and one-half         367) Tj T*
(years without a shut down.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Plant B.--This plant, which is located in the center of a peat bog,) Tj T*
(proved of especial interest. It has a capacity of 300 horsepower only,) Tj T*
(and is about 3 miles from the town to which the electric current is) Tj T*
(supplied. One-half of the plant \(150 horsepower\) was installed in 1904) Tj T*
(and the remainder in 1906. This is probably the first as well as the) Tj T*
(smallest producer-gas installation to be located at the mine and) Tj T*
(transmit high-voltage current to a point some distance away. This) Tj T*
(installation, in 1909, consisted of two suction producers \(special) Tj T*
(peat type\) rated at 150 horsepower each, and two horizontal twin) Tj T*
(single-acting four-cycle gas engines of 150 horsepower each, direct) Tj T*
(connected to alternating-current three-phase generators, which were) Tj T*
(running splendidly in parallel at the time of my visit. The 3,000-volt) Tj T*
(current is transmitted to the town, where it is used during the day) Tj T*
(for lighting shops and for shop motors. At night the plant supplies) Tj T*
(the lights for the streets and residences. The charge for residence) Tj T*
(light is 9 cents per kilowatt hour. Both units are in operation from) Tj T*
(5:30 a. m. to 6 p. m., and one continues to 11 p. m. each day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A 35-horsepower peat machine is used for preparing the fuel. This is) Tj T*
(driven by an electric motor supplied with current from the power plant) Tj T*
(on the bog. As only 750 tons of dry peat are required per year there) Tj T*
(is no attempt to work the plant to its maximum. Local farmers are) Tj T*
(employed and they work as little or as much as they please, as there) Tj T*
(is no difficulty in getting out all the peat needed for a year during) Tj T*
(the working season, which in this locality is from April 15 to) Tj T*
(September 1. As a result 14 men are employed more or less of their) Tj T*
(time. They receive about 50 cents per day each and get out about 20) Tj T*
(tons of peat per day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Coal at this point in Europe costs $3.75 per ton. The dry peat           368) Tj T*
(delivered on the operating platform of the producer plant costs only) Tj T*
(80 cents per ton.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
