(the equipment. The engines in use were direct connected to electric) Tj T*
(generators. The 10,000-volt current is used for operating the local) Tj T*
(mine machinery and also for furnishing lights for neighboring towns) Tj T*
(and power for a street railroad. The plant was reported to be using) Tj T*
(over 100 tons of this low-grade fuel per day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Favorable Conditions in the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the United States cheaper power is constantly sought. The) Tj T*
(water-power possibilities of the country are being realized and the) Tj T*
(hydro-electric power plant is a wholesome cause of competition. The) Tj T*
(supply of fuel of marketable grades is not unlimited. Prices for such) Tj T*
(fuel must necessarily increase. The cost of transporting coal from the) Tj T*
(mines is high, and the possibility of obtaining a sufficient supply of) Tj T*
(cars to handle low-grade fuels is questionable. The power demands of) Tj T*
(the country are increasing, and this power must be developed at a) Tj T*
(reasonable cost. The time is approaching when the cheapest fuel) Tj T*
(obtainable must be used to the best economic advantage in order to) Tj T*
(develop power at a unit cost consistent with commercial progress.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Consideration of the conditions indicates that in order to keep the      369) Tj T*
(price of power developed from fuel down to a consistent figure--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(a\) Grades of fuel which warrant transportation, or which may be) Tj T*
(defined as ?marketable,? should be used with the greatest possible) Tj T*
(practicable economy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\) The very large percentage of coal of so-called low grade which) Tj T*
(today is left at or in the mine must be utilized.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(c\) Advantage must be taken of the large deposits of lignite and peat) Tj T*
(which are found in many sections of the country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is undoubtedly true that in general, under conditions which do not) Tj T*
(require the use of steam for other than power purposes, the) Tj T*
(producer-gas power plant meets the requirements of \(a\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At present the only method of advantageously handling the fuels) Tj T*
(mentioned in \(b\) and \(c\) is in the gas producer, and the utilization) Tj T*
(of these lower grades of fuel on an extensive scale demands) Tj T*
(concentration of the power plants within close proximity to the fuel) Tj T*
(supply.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The logical conclusion from a careful study of the producer-gas power) Tj T*
(situation is that the time is not distant when financial interests in) Tj T*
(power production will be directed toward the centralization of the) Tj T*
(producer-gas power plant at the mines and the distribution of the) Tj T*
(energy developed either by high-voltage long-distance electrical) Tj T*
(transmission or by pipe systems for conveying the gas.) Tj T*
ET
