() Tj T*
(2. It is only recently that educational institutions have afforded       373) Tj T*
(any opportunity for adequate instruction in the art of management,) Tj T*
(pure and simple, a principal feature of which is the intelligent) Tj T*
(regulation of cost.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. There has been, and now is, as a result of these two things, a) Tj T*
(failure to appreciate the necessity and value of exact data, in proper) Tj T*
(terms, of refined and scientific methods of collecting and using it) Tj T*
(and of logical reasoning in the solution of industrial problems.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The highest degree of efficiency, therefore, is only to be realized in) Tj T*
(a shop where executive methods have reached a high stage of) Tj T*
(efficiency, for in these is unquestionably its source.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Time Measurement Important.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first step is to recognize the necessity and value of a proper) Tj T*
(measurement of time, as a guide not only to the executive but to the) Tj T*
(workman. A man was observed during 8 successive repetitions of the) Tj T*
(operation of making a machine mold in a foundry. The unit times varied) Tj T*
(5.2 to 23.6 minutes, the total time for the eight being 104 minutes.) Tj T*
(Under the method of timekeeping in use at that shop it was only) Tj T*
(ascertained that the eight operations took 1æ hours or an ?average? of) Tj T*
(13 minutes each, and the labor cost and distribution of burden were) Tj T*
(made on that basis. Because of the absence of any standard time) Tj T*
(whatsoever it was not realized that had the man done each of the eight) Tj T*
(in 5.2 minutes, they would have been completed in 41.6 minutes,) Tj T*
(resulting in a saving of over 60 per cent of the total time. Had the) Tj T*
(man received a proper work ticket bearing this standard time, before) Tj T*
(he began the work, there is no doubt that he could have easily) Tj T*
(performed the work in the shorter time and a marked difference in) Tj T*
(proportionate burden and cost would have resulted. Under the existing) Tj T*
(methods the management could not know of the waste, and so was) Tj T*
(helpless to prevent or cure it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Every item of time, therefore, is capable of division into two parts:    374) Tj T*
(A standard or necessary time and a \(more or less\) preventable waste,) Tj T*
(which latter is the easier thing of the two to determine.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An Example of Increased Efficiency in Riveting.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A gang of four were engaged in riveting some steel plates. By the use) Tj T*
(of a stop-watch it was found that a large proportion of the total time) Tj T*
(of the riveter and bucker-up was not utilized; yet some one was always) Tj T*
(at work. The reason was that the men proceeded along the work in such) Tj T*
(a way that the bucker-up covered with his body the holes as yet) Tj T*
(unfilled by rivets, he moving from left to right. When, therefore, a) Tj T*
