(One thing more: Much has been done and overdone in the line of) Tj T*
(so-called welfare work. It is a highly creditable and necessary line) Tj T*
(of effort, when confined to attempts to remove from the path of the) Tj T*
(employe any obstacle which prevents him from developing his skill and) Tj T*
(efficiency to the highest degree. An uncomfortable, unhappy person) Tj T*
(cannot be efficient. But as steam is necessary to the engine, so is) Tj T*
(incentive necessary to the worker to get him to make the best use of) Tj T*
(the facilities provided for him. Under our present civilization, the) Tj T*
(same incentive which pushes on the master will push on the man, and) Tj T*
(that is direct personal gain in dollars and cents, not for itself, but) Tj T*
(for and what that gain will bring. It must come to him quickly after) Tj T*
(the exertion which its expectation calls forth, for if long delayed,) Tj T*
(the effect is lost. It must also come to him separately from his) Tj T*
(regular wage that its amount may be the more readily realized.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Moreover, the results of efficiency methods, within the writer?s) Tj T*
(knowledge, are sufficient to convince him that their general adoption) Tj T*
(would so increase the purchasing power of the employe, by increasing) Tj T*
(his wages and decreasing the cost production, as to have a markedly) Tj T*
(beneficial and steadying effect upon the business of the country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
