(and to mark the point at which they diverge. The employer and the) Tj T*
(employe are mutually interested in the successful conduct of industry;) Tj T*
(the profits of the one and the wages of the other obviously are) Tj T*
(contingent upon it, as both profits and wages must be paid from the) Tj T*
(earnings of the enterprise in which the capital of the one and the) Tj T*
(labor of the other are jointly invested. This being true, the workman) Tj T*
(and the employer are equally concerned in the character of the product) Tj T*
(which is manufactured and sold by them, just as they are interested) Tj T*
(equally in good markets and regularity of employment. Having worked in) Tj T*
(co-operation up to the point of turning out an article that commands a) Tj T*
(wide and profitable sale, the question of dividing the earnings of) Tj T*
(their joint efforts presents itself. It is the failure of the attempt) Tj T*
(to adjust satisfactorily this controversy that gives rise to the         381) Tj T*
(differences between employers and workmen and is the basis of the) Tj T*
(labor problem as we have it today. True, there are many questions of) Tj T*
(discord apart from those of wages and profits, which result in serious) Tj T*
(industrial conflicts, but followed back to their source, it will be) Tj T*
(found that these issues are inseparably related to those of wages and) Tj T*
(profits. In other words, the demand for a shorter workday, for) Tj T*
(healthful, sanitary surroundings, has its origin in the irrepressible) Tj T*
(desire of the working people for a progressive improvement in their) Tj T*
(conditions of life and labor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In ancient and mediaeval times when the structure of society was) Tj T*
(simple and each family consumed all the things it produced; or even at) Tj T*
(a later period when the master and the journeyman worked together side) Tj T*
(by side, and when the master had been a journeyman and the journeyman) Tj T*
(expected to become a master, there was little cause for controversy,) Tj T*
(and the problem of labor was not difficult of solution. It was not) Tj T*
(until the invention of machinery, the advent of the factory system,) Tj T*
(the use of steam, and the application of new processes that the) Tj T*
(question of the relationship of employer and employed grew so complex) Tj T*
(and impersonal that new methods became necessary in the proper) Tj T*
(adjustment of industrial affairs. As step by step industry developed) Tj T*
(from the stage of the privately owned factory to the firm and) Tj T*
(corporation, to the combination and the trust, the real employer was) Tj T*
(removed further and ever further from personal contact with his) Tj T*
(employes. As a consequence of this transition, the salaried manager) Tj T*
(took the place once held by the actual employer, and the simple and) Tj T*
(friendly relations of early days gave way to the intricate and complex) Tj T*
(industrial life of this generation.) Tj T*
